      "content": "You are an Expert Human SOP Faithfulness Inspector for an IT Automation System.\n\nYour task is to perform a rigorous Chain-of-Thought (CoT) inspection completely comparing a Raw Human SOP document text against a Converted OKF Steps JSON.\n\n## RAW HUMAN SOP TEXT:\nSOP-L1-APP-001\nSoftware Application Unblock Request\n\nSTANDARD OPERATING PROCEDURE\n\nSoftware Application Unblock\n\nRequest\n\nEndpoint Support  →  Application Management\n\nSOP ID\nSOP-L1-APP-001\n\nSupport Level\nL1 Service Desk\n\nCategory\nEndpoint Support / Application Management\n\nPrimary Remediation Path\nIFEO Debugger Entry Removal\n\nDocument Version\n1.0\n\nStatus\nApproved for Use\n\nClassification\nInternal Use Only\n\nThis document defines the standard, command-based process for identifying an\napplication block caused by an Image File Execution Options (IFEO) debugger entry\n\nand removing it as a fallback remediation on a Windows endpoint.\n\nIT Service Desk — Confidential / Internal Use Only\nPage 1\n\nSOP-L1-APP-001\nSoftware Application Unblock Request\n\n.  Table of Contents\n\n1.\nObjective\n\n2.\nPreconditions\n\n3.\nProcess Flow Overview\n\n4.\nDetailed Procedure\n\nStep 1 — Verify Endpoint Connectivity\n\nStep 2 — Identify Application Blocking Mechanism\n\nStep 3 — Remove IFEO Block (Fallback)\n\nStep 4 — Refresh Local Policy\n\nStep 5 — Verify Block Removal\n\nStep 6 — Validate Resolution\n\nStep 7 — Update Ticket\n\n5.\nEscalation Criteria\n\n6.\nDocument Control\n\nIT Service Desk — Confidential / Internal Use Only\nPage 2\n\nSOP-L1-APP-001\nSoftware Application Unblock Request\n\n1.  Objective\n\nRestore access to an approved software application that is blocked on a Windows endpoint by identifying the\nblocking mechanism and applying the appropriate remediation. If the block is caused by an Image File\nExecution Options (IFEO) debugger entry, remove the entry as a fallback remediation.\n\n2.  Preconditions\n\n•\nTicket assigned to L1 Engineer.\n\n•\nRemote administrative access to the endpoint.\n\n•\nUser device is online.\n\n•\nAdministrative privileges available.\n\n3.  Process Flow Overview\n\nThe diagram below summarizes the end-to-end decision flow. Full instructions for each stage are provided in\nSection 4, Detailed Procedure.\n\n1. Verify\nConnectivity\n→\n2. Identify Blocking\nMechanism\n→\n3–5. Remove, Refresh\n& Verify\n\nIs the application blocked via an IFEO Debugger entry? (Step 2)\n\nYES — IFEO Debugger Entry Found\nNO — Registry Key Not Found\n\nProceed to Step 3 — remove the Debugger entry\n(and the key itself if it exists solely to block the app),\nthen refresh policy and verify.\n\nApplication is not blocked through IFEO. Investigate\nAppLocker, WDAC, Intune, or Endpoint Security\npolicies, or escalate to L2.\n\nIT Service Desk — Confidential / Internal Use Only\nPage 3\n\nSOP-L1-APP-001\nSoftware Application Unblock Request\n\n4.  Detailed Procedure\n\nSTEP 1  —  Verify Endpoint Connectivity\n\nCommand\n\nTest-Connection <ComputerName> -Count 2\n\n\u0014 Expected Result: Reply received from target system.\n\nIf unreachable — Action:\n\n•\nVerify VPN / network connectivity.\n\n•\nRetry.\n\n•\nEscalate if unreachable.\n\nSTEP 2  —  Identify Application Blocking Mechanism\n\nCommand\n\nreg query \"HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Image File Execution Options\\<Application>.exe\"\n\nExpected Result 1\n\nDebugger    REG_SZ    ...\n\nResult: Application is blocked using IFEO. Proceed to Step 3.\n\nExpected Result 2\n\nERROR:\nThe system was unable to find the specified registry key.\n\nResult: Application is not blocked through IFEO. Investigate other blocking technologies (AppLocker, WDAC,\nIntune, Endpoint Security) or escalate to L2.\n\nSTEP 3  —  Remove IFEO Block (Fallback)\n\nExecute only when Step 2 confirms an IFEO Debugger entry.\n\nRemove Debugger Value\n\nreg delete \"HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Image File Execution Options\\<Application>.exe\" ^\n  /v Debugger /f\n\nIf the application-specific IFEO key was created only for blocking, remove the key:\n\nreg delete \"HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Image File Execution Options\\<Application>.exe\" ^\n  /f\n\nSTEP 4  —  Refresh Local Policy\n\nCommand\n\ngpupdate /force\n\n\u0014 Expected Result: Computer Policy update has completed successfully. User Policy update has completed\nsuccessfully.\n\nIT Service Desk — Confidential / Internal Use Only\nPage 4\n\nSOP-L1-APP-001\nSoftware Application Unblock Request\n\nSTEP 5  —  Verify Block Removal\n\nCommand\n\nreg query \"HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Image File Execution Options\\<Application>.exe\"\n\n\u0014 Expected Result: ERROR: The system was unable to find the specified registry key — or — Debugger\nvalue not present.\n\nSTEP 6  —  Validate Resolution\n\nAsk the user to launch the application.\n\n\u0014 Expected Result:\n\n•\nApplication launches successfully.\n\n•\nNo error message displayed.\n\n•\nUser confirms issue resolved.\n\nIf the application remains blocked:\n\n•\nCheck for AppLocker policies.\n\n•\nCheck WDAC policies.\n\n•\nCheck Endpoint Security policies.\n\n•\nEscalate to L2 Support.\n\nSTEP 7  —  Update Ticket\n\nResolution Notes\n\nIssue:\nApplication launch blocked.\n\nRoot Cause:\nIFEO Debugger registry entry prevented application execution.\n\nAction Taken:\nVerified IFEO configuration.\nRemoved Debugger registry entry.\nRefreshed Group Policy.\nValidated successful application launch.\n\nStatus:\nResolved.\n\nIT Service Desk — Confidential / Internal Use Only\nPage 5\n\nSOP-L1-APP-001\nSoftware Application Unblock Request\n\n5.  Escalation Criteria\n\nEscalate to L2 if:\n\n•\nIFEO key not present.\n\n•\nApplication blocked by WDAC.\n\n•\nApplication blocked by AppLocker.\n\n•\nEndpoint protection policy prevents execution.\n\n•\nRegistry modification fails.\n\n•\nUser lacks required permissions.\n\n•\nApplication still fails after remediation.\n\n6.  Document Control\n\nAttribute\nValue\n\nSOP ID\nSOP-L1-APP-001\n\nTitle\nSoftware Application Unblock Request\n\nCategory\nEndpoint Support → Application Management\n\nSupport Level\nL1 Service Desk\n\nPrimary Remediation Path\nIFEO Debugger Entry Removal\n\nVersion\n1.0\n\nStatus\nApproved for use\n\nIT Service Desk — Confidential / Internal Use Only\nPage 6\n\n## CONVERTED OKF STEPS JSON:\n[\n  {\n    \"step_number\": 1,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Verify endpoint connectivity using Test-Connection.\",\n    \"step_type\": \"command\",\n    \"step_reasoning\": \"Gate 1-4 all failed for tool_call, as this step uses a native CLI command (Test-Connection). The command is directly translated from the SOP, with {{entities.computer_name}} as a dynamic placeholder for the target endpoint.\",\n    \"platform\": null,\n    \"function_name\": null,\n    \"comm_inputs\": null,\n    \"command\": \"Test-Connection {{entities.computer_name}} -Count 2\",\n    \"fallback_command\": null,\n    \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n    \"parse_instruction\": null,\n    \"execute_if\": null,\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 30\n  },\n  {\n    \"step_number\": 2,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Identify if the application is blocked by an IFEO Debugger entry.\",\n    \"step_type\": \"command\",\n    \"step_reasoning\": \"Gate 1-4 all failed for tool_call, as this step uses a native CLI command (reg query). The command is directly translated from the SOP, with {{entities.application_exe}} as a dynamic placeholder for the blocked application executable.\",\n    \"platform\": null,\n    \"function_name\": null,\n    \"comm_inputs\": null,\n    \"command\": \"reg query \\\"HKLM\\\\SOFTWARE\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows NT\\\\CurrentVersion\\\\Image File Execution Options\\\\{{entities.application_exe}}\\\"\",\n    \"fallback_command\": null,\n    \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n    \"parse_instruction\": null,\n    \"execute_if\": null,\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 30\n  },\n  {\n    \"step_number\": 3,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Remove the IFEO Debugger entry if confirmed in Step 2.\",\n    \"step_type\": \"command\",\n    \"step_reasoning\": \"Gate 1-4 all failed for tool_call, as this step uses a native CLI command (reg delete). The command is directly translated from the SOP, with {{entities.application_exe}} as a dynamic placeholder. This step executes only if Step 2 confirms an IFEO block (execute_if: variables.ifeo_block_confirmed == 'true').\",\n    \"platform\": null,\n    \"function_name\": null,\n    \"comm_inputs\": null,\n    \"command\": \"reg delete \\\"HKLM\\\\SOFTWARE\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows NT\\\\CurrentVersion\\\\Image File Execution Options\\\\{{entities.application_exe}}\\\" /v Debugger /f\",\n    \"fallback_command\": \"reg delete \\\"HKLM\\\\SOFTWARE\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows NT\\\\CurrentVersion\\\\Image File Execution Options\\\\{{entities.application_exe}}\\\" /f\",\n    \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n    \"parse_instruction\": null,\n    \"execute_if\": \"variables.ifeo_block_confirmed == 'true'\",\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 60\n  },\n  {\n    \"step_number\": 4,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Refresh local Group Policy to apply changes.\",\n    \"step_type\": \"command\",\n    \"step_reasoning\": \"Gate 1-4 all failed for tool_call, as this step uses a native CLI command (gpupdate /force). The command is directly translated from the SOP and executes unconditionally after the IFEO block removal.\",\n    \"platform\": null,\n    \"function_name\": null,\n    \"comm_inputs\": null,\n    \"command\": \"gpupdate /force\",\n    \"fallback_command\": null,\n    \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n    \"parse_instruction\": null,\n    \"execute_if\": null,\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 90\n  },\n  {\n    \"step_number\": 5,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Verify that the IFEO Debugger entry has been removed.\",\n    \"step_type\": \"command\",\n    \"step_reasoning\": \"Gate 1-4 all failed for tool_call, as this step uses a native CLI command (reg query). The command is directly translated from the SOP, with {{entities.application_exe}} as a dynamic placeholder. This step executes only if Step 2 confirmed an IFEO block (execute_if: variables.ifeo_block_confirmed == 'true').\",\n    \"platform\": null,\n    \"function_name\": null,\n    \"comm_inputs\": null,\n    \"command\": \"reg query \\\"HKLM\\\\SOFTWARE\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows NT\\\\CurrentVersion\\\\Image File Execution Options\\\\{{entities.application_exe}}\\\"\",\n    \"fallback_command\": null,\n    \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n    \"parse_instruction\": null,\n    \"execute_if\": \"variables.ifeo_block_confirmed == 'true'\",\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 30\n  }\n]\n\n## MANDATORY CoT INSPECTION CHECKS:\nBefore outputting the final verdict, complete these 3 inspection reasoning checks in order:\n\n- **Check 1 (100% Action & Tool Recall & Preservation)**: Verify that EVERY SINGLE automated procedure step described in the raw human text (whether a shell CLI command like `ipconfig`/`chkdsk` OR an API tool action like `unlock_user_account`/`admin_reset_password`) is preserved in the OKF steps. If any automated action or tool call is missing from the OKF steps, you MUST mark `is_faithful = false` and add it to `dropped_commands`.\n  *(HUMAN CONFIRMATION EXEMPTION: Human/verbal/ticket confirmations, user clarifications, and manual admin approval steps are currently PAUSED. DO NOT flag omitted verbal/ticket/user confirmation steps as dropped commands.)*\n  *(GUI SETUP EXEMPTION: GUI setup steps such as \"Open Command Prompt\", \"Press Windows Key\", \"Run as administrator\", \"Open Web Browser\", or opening UI windows are intentionally omitted from executable playbooks. DO NOT flag GUI setup steps or UI window launches as dropped commands.)*\n  *(TOOL PARAMETER MAPPING EXEMPTION: When an automated search or query step maps to a registered API tool whose interface requires a specific input key (such as `search_users` requiring `email`), passing the query entity like `{{entities.email}}` or `{{entities.partial_detail}}` in `comm_inputs` satisfies the step. Do NOT flag other raw search criteria like name or employee ID as dropped commands or parameter inaccuracies when mapping to a catalog tool's defined input parameters.)*\n- **Check 2 (Hallucination Prevention)**: Verify that NO extra CLI commands or fabricated API tool calls were created that were NOT in the raw human SOP text.\n- **Check 3 (Fallback & Parameter Accuracy)**: Verify that fallback commands (`fallback_command`), cross-SOP referrals (`fallback_sop_id`), and tool inputs match the raw text's instructions within the constraints of the registered API tools.\n- **Check 4 (4 Verification Gates & Command Executability Audit)**:\n  * For EVERY `tool_call` step: Verify it satisfies the 4 Gates (Gate 1: matches declared platform function, Gate 2: valid platform, Gate 3: problem aligned, Gate 4: required input parameters present in `comm_inputs`).\n  * For EVERY `command` step: Verify that `command` is an actual executable CLI string and is NEVER null or empty.\n  * Verify that purely manual/verbal/phone relay steps were NOT emitted as empty command steps.\n- **Check 5 (Validation Confidence Scoring)**:\n  * `confidence_score`: Decimal between 0.0 and 1.0 evaluating your confidence in this faithfulness inspection (e.g. 1.0 for completely clear SOP comparison, 0.80 if minor ambiguities, 0.50 if highly ambiguous).\n  * `confidence_level`: \"High\" (>= 0.85), \"Medium\" (0.60 - 0.84), or \"Low\" (< 0.60).\n  * `confidence_reason`: Brief rationale for the validation confidence score.\n\n## VERDICT CONTRACT:\n- If all actions are preserved, zero hallucinated commands/tools exist, and all steps are 100% executable, set `is_faithful = true` and `validation_feedback = \"PASSED FAITHFULNESS INSPECTION\"`.\n- If any actions are missing, fabricated, or non-executable, set `is_faithful = false` and populate `dropped_commands` or `hallucinated_commands`.\n- Always provide `confidence_score`, `confidence_level`, and `confidence_reason`.\n\nOutput a valid JSON object matching the JITFaithfulnessInspectionResult schema.\n"
    }
  ]
